# Auth Layer

`src/auth/` is the Strategy layer for JWT, opaque, and OAuth. Entities never import it.

## Public construction

`Bling.create({ baseUrl?, auth })` with discriminated `auth.method`:

- `jwt` — Bearer + `enable-jwt: 1` on resource calls; no `.auth`.
- `opaque` — Bearer only (legacy); no `.auth`.
- `oauth` — `OAuthClient` on `BlingOAuthClient.auth`; always JWT for token exchange and resource calls. **Server-side only.**

No `tokenFormat` option. OAuth always sends `enable-jwt: 1` on `POST /oauth/token`.

## Internals

| Piece | Role |
|-------|------|
| `IAuthProvider` | `applyRequestHeaders`; optional `ensureFreshToken`, `handleUnauthorized` |
| `JwtAuthProvider` / `OpaqueAuthProvider` / `OAuthAuthProvider` | Concrete strategies |
| `createAuthProvider` | Sole `auth.method` switch |
| `OAuthClient` | authorize URL, code exchange, refresh, revoke |
| Defaults | Resource `https://api.bling.com.br/Api/v3`; OAuth `https://www.bling.com.br/Api/v3` |

Coalesce in-flight refresh when `autoRefresh` is on. Basic auth on token/revoke **headers only**. Reuse `BlingApiException` / `BlingInternalException`. Do not parse JWT payloads.

Revoke body: `token`, `token_type_hint`; advanced `revoke_action` (`logout` \| `uninstall`) and `revoke_target` (`user` \| `company`).

## Tests

Colocate under `src/auth/**/__tests__`. Mock axios; do not hit live Bling.
